web image smoke	Build web image	2026-08-29T17:12:52.3830402Z             "body": "Closes the \"visual regression\" tier `00-DISCOVERY.md` listed as missing, using\nPlaywright's own `toHaveScreenshot` on WO-21's harness. No new dependency, no\nhosted service, no approval UI, no lockfile change.\n\n## The three criteria, mapped to evidence\n\n### 1. Snapshots for the five slice steps plus the degraded states with retained baseline screenshots\n\n`web/e2e/visual.spec.ts` — **48 committed PNGs**, 12 renders × light/dark ×\n412/1440 px, 3,257,408 B total (avg 66 KiB), in\n`web/e2e/__screenshots__/darwin/`.\n\n| Half | State | Slice step (`05` §2.1) | Retained Gate 1 screenshot |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| slice | `landing` | 1 — new question | `home-desktop-full.png`, `home-mobile-full.png` |\n| slice | `running` | 2 — reload-safe job | `running-desktop.png` |\n| slice | `plan-review` | 3 — plan review | `plan-review-desktop.png`, `plan-review-mobile-full.png` |\n| slice | `reconnecting` | 4 — stream and reconnect | `reconnecting-desktop.png` |\n| slice | `thread-populated` | 5 — report, metrics, export | `conversation-populated-desktop-full.png` (+ dark, + mobile) |\n| degraded | `cancelled` | — | `cancelled-desktop.png` |\n| degraded | `failed-partial` | — | `failed-partial-desktop.png`, `failed-partial-mobile.png` |\n| degraded | `expired` | — | `expired-job-desktop.png` |\n| degraded | `submission-error-500` | — | `submission-error-desktop.png` |\n| degraded | `rail-error-upstream` | — | `backend-offline-desktop.png` |\n| degraded | `thread-not-found-inline` | — | `conversation-not-found-desktop.png` |\n| degraded | `route-not-found` | — | `framework-not-found-desktop.png` |\n\n**Why seven degraded states and not \"the four\".** Nothing in `06`, `05` or `00`\nnames which four, and the arithmetic does not produce four on the state table\nWO-21 built. Thirteen of the twenty `states.ts` rows are degraded; **seven** of\nthose have a retained Gate 1 capture to compare against (the other six —\n`rail-error-proxy-503`, `failed-no-result`, `rate-limited-429`,\n`unauthorized-401`, `validation-422`, `attached-status-unknown` — postdate the\nGate 1 evidence run; `env.ts` says exactly that of `failed-no-result`). Of the\nseven, two are reached inside the slice (`expired` is step 2's second half,\n`failed-partial` is step 5's), which leaves *five*, not four. Rather than pick\none reading and silently drop the rest, the suite covers all seven: every\nreading of the criterion is then a subset of what is here, and the surplus is\nthree states' worth of PNG. The reasoning is on `DEGRADED_STATES` in the spec.\n\nThree things are asserted rather than described, so the inventory cannot rot:\n\n- every named retained baseline screenshot **exists on disk** under\n  `docs/revamp/baseline/screenshots/`;\n- the five slice steps are covered once each and no degraded state is also\n  claimed as a slice step;\n- the sweep is 12 × 2 × 2 and no two renders would write the same file.\n\nTwo states needed more than a URL. `reconnecting` (§4 row 11) is in\n`DEFERRED_STATES` because it is a transition, but it has a resting *appearance*\n— the browser's own `EventSource` retry holds the spine there — and Gate 1\ncaptured it for that reason; it uses `interruptStream`, the technique\n`capture-baseline.spec.ts:63-76` already proved. `submission-error-500` renders\n`landing`'s pixels until something is actually submitted, so it submits, and\n`POST /api/research` is additionally aborted at the route for that one render on\ntop of the three structural cost mechanisms.\n\n### 2. A deliberate 2 px shift fails the check\n\nIntroduced by appending `main#main,[data-thread-rail]{padding-top:2px}` to the\nserved stylesheet through `page.route` — **not** `addStyleTag`, which WO-30's\n`style-src 'self'` blocks. As far as the browser is concerned, the stylesheet\nshipped 2 px of padding.\n\n```\n  48 failed\n  5 passed (38.7s)\n```\n\n```\n  1) [chromium] › e2e/visual.spec.ts › … › landing · light · 412px (§4 1) @visual\n\n    Error: expect(page).toHaveScreenshot(expected) failed\n\n      4551 pixels (ratio 0.02 of all image pixels) are different.\n\n      Snapshot: landing-light-412.png\n```\n\nAll **48 of 48** snapshot comparisons went red; the 5 that passed are the\ninventory tests, which do not take a picture. Per-render deltas ranged from\n**1,441 to 13,703 pixels** — the smallest is 7.2× the tolerance and the largest\n68×.\n\nA first pass shifted only `main#main` and produced **46** failures: the two that\npassed were `rail-error-upstream` at 412, where the rail drawer is a modal over\n`main`, so no shifted pixel was on screen. That is the gate measuring pixels\nrather than asserting blindly, and the demonstration was widened to cover the\ndrawer.\n\nReverted in the same session; the suite is green on this branch (below).\n\n### 3. The depth limit is recorded\n\n`docs/revamp/evidence/gate-4/residual-risks.md` — new, created as the stub\nWO-33 extends. Entries are `RR-NN` with seven fixed fields and an index table,\nso the remaining three risks §4.2 names (field CWV, browser matrix limits, the\nMT-01 dependency) append without restructuring.\n\n> **RR-01 — Visual-regression coverage is the slice, not the matrix.**\n> *Risk:* a visual regression in a state the snapshot suite does not cover ships\n> unnoticed. *Covered:* 48 PNGs — the five slice steps plus every degraded state\n> with a retained Gate 1 screenshot, in light and dark at 412 and 1440, Chromium\n> on `darwin`. *Not covered:* the other nine `states.ts` rows, 320 px, every\n> `DEFERRED_STATES` transition, Firefox and WebKit, forced-colours,\n> reduced-motion as a separate axis, every Storybook story, and — until a\n> `linux` set is generated and reviewed — the CI runner, where the sweep skips\n> rather than gates. *Why accepted:*\n> the matrix is 20 × 2 × 3 = 120 renders, ~8 MB of committed binary that one\n> legitimate token change invalidates in a single commit — the cost of a visual\n> baseline is not taking it but re-taking it, and re-taking 120 files by hand is\n> how a team learns to run `--update-snapshots` without looking; this is a\n> single-deployment product with no per-tenant CSS (MT-01); the nine uncovered\n> states are still swept by axe in both themes at three widths, measured for\n> reflow, and rendered as Storybook stories, so what is missing for them is\n> pixel comparison specifically; and Chromium/`darwin` only is the same argument\n> one level down, because a snapshot's artefact *is* the engine's rasterisation.\n> *What would change it:* per-tenant theming; a visual regression reaching a\n> user in an uncovered state; literal values leaking out of the token layer; or\n> CI gaining a Linux leg somebody actually reviews.\n\n## The update workflow\n\n```bash\nnpm run e2e:visual            # compare against the committed set\nnpm run e2e:visual:update     # regenerate\n```\n\n`web/e2e/README.md` gains a \"Visual regression (WO-28)\" section stating when\nregeneration is legitimate — **you changed how something looks, on purpose, and\nthe new pixels ship in the same PR as the change that produced them** — and\nwhen it is not: an unexpected red run (that is the gate working; open the\nthree-up diff in `web/build/e2e/report/`), a red run on a platform that did not\nproduce the set (generate that platform's own directory instead), or flake (the\nfix is a determinism measure, not fresh bytes or a wider tolerance).\n\n## Determinism\n\nEight measures, each with the drift it removes, tabulated in the README and\ndocumented on `settleForCapture()`:\n\n1. **no `[data-skeleton-lines]` on screen** — the measure that was missing. A\n   skeleton is *static*, so a DOM-quiescence check agrees with itself and\n   photographs a page still waiting for its data. The suite flaked on its own\n   second run for exactly this: `landing` captured with the rail's two threads\n   loaded, then with the rail's two skeleton bars, 527 pixels apart.\n2. `settleForAudit` — WO-22's DOM-quiescence loop, reused rather than re-written.\n3. `document.fonts.ready`, then `fonts.status` asserted (it also resolves on\n   failure) — the faces are self-hosted with `font-display: swap`.\n4. two `requestAnimationFrame`s.\n5. `emulateMedia({ colorScheme, reducedMotion: \"reduce\" })` before navigation —\n   the theme axis without `localStorage`, because `theme.spec.ts` pins a live\n   hydration defect that would capture dark states in light.\n6. `animations: \"disabled\"`, `caret: \"hide\"`, `scale: \"css\"`, `fullPage: false`,\n   passed explicitly.\n7. seeded `baseline-*` fixtures only.\n8. Chromium only (`@visual` joins `CHROMIUM_ONLY`), and `{platform}` in\n   `snapshotPathTemplate` so a second OS is additive rather than a conflict.\n\n**Results.**\n\n- Four consecutive full runs from a clean stack: **53 passed** each time\n  (48 snapshots + 5 inventory tests).\n- Byte-level: **45 of 48 byte-identical** between two forced regenerations; the\n  other three (`plan-review-light-1440`, `rail-error-upstream-dark-412`,\n  `submission-error-500-dark-412`) differ by **4, 9 and 14 raw pixels**, below\n  Playwright's per-pixel threshold, so the comparator never counts them.\n- `maxDiffPixels` is **200**, and it is the one tolerance in the file. Six full\n  zero-tolerance runs (288 comparisons) produced exactly one render that the\n  comparator ever saw move: `thread-populated` at 1440, bimodally 124 px (dark)\n  / 131 px (light). Cause measured, not guessed: the briefing's `SectionRail` is\n  `position: sticky` above 1280 px and lays out at x = 1007.46875 — probed\n  twelve times, identical rect, colour, weight and `aria-current` every time —\n  and a sticky box is a compositor-promotion candidate, so its glyphs are\n  rasterised snapped to 1007 or unsnapped at 1007.47, half a pixel apart.\n  `--disable-lcd-text` was tried and measured: it makes no difference, because\n  this is subpixel *positioning* rather than the choice of antialiasing.\n  Masking the rail and injecting `position: static` were both rejected for\n  taking a real surface out of the gate. The tolerance bounds *area* rather than\n  raising `threshold`, so a colour change over a whole surface stays red however\n  small its per-pixel delta.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | clean |\n| `npm run test` | 135 files, **3026 passed**, 7 skipped |\n| `npm run budgets` (build + budgets) | all rows PASS, no ratchet |\n| `npm run audit:gate` | 0 high/critical in the production tree; 3 dev-tree, all pre-accounted |\n| `npm run contract:check` | generated types match `contract/openapi.json` |\n| `npm run e2e -- --project=chromium` | see below |\n| `npm run e2e:visual` × 4 | 53 passed each (54 after the skip guard landed) |\n| 2 px shift | 48/48 snapshot comparisons red |\n\nRun against an isolated stack — Compose project `arxiv-wo28-e2e`, containers\n`arxiv-wo28-{app,web,redis,postgres}`, ports 13280/18280 — so the two sibling\nGate 4 branches were untouched. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=local-preview-disabled`\nthroughout; **no paid model call was made**, and `submission-error-500` is the\nonly render that submits anything, with `POST /api/research` aborted at the\nroute on top of the three existing structural mechanisms.\n\n## For the coordinator: CI\n\n**No workflow was edited.** `@visual` is grepped into the existing `chromium`\nproject, so `npm run e2e -- --project=chromium` — the command the `web-e2e` job\nalready runs — picks the suite up with no new step.\n\n**On the Linux runner the forty-eight comparisons currently SKIP, on purpose.**\n`e2e/__screenshots__/linux/` does not exist, and the three things that could\nhappen there are: fail all forty-eight for the absence of bytes nobody wrote (a\nred build that means \"no baseline\", not \"regression\"); let the runner write its\nown and pass (a baseline the runner produced and then immediately agreed with,\nwhich proves nothing, and is the worse of the two); or skip with a message\nnaming the platform, the directory and the command that fixes it. The suite\ndoes the third. `--update-snapshots` turns the skip off, because that *is* the\nrequest to generate a set.\n\nThe skip is guarded: one test in the file never skips, so deleting the\n`__screenshots__` tree turns the suite red rather than quiet, and every run\nlogs which sets exist and whether this platform is gating or skipping —\n\n```\n[visual] committed baseline sets: darwin; this run is \"linux\" (SKIPPING — no set).\n  48 skipped\n  6 passed\n```\n\nSo the gate is real on a developer's macOS and inert on the runner today. That\nis a second residual limit and RR-01 says so rather than leaving it to be\ndiscovered. Two decisions belong to whoever owns CI, written up at the foot of\n`web/e2e/README.md`:\n\n- **To make it gate on CI**, generate `e2e/__screenshots__/linux/` on a Linux\n  host (`mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.62.1-noble` against the seeded stack,\n  or the runner itself with a one-off `--update-snapshots`), **look at the\n  forty-eight images**, and commit them. The suite activates with no code\n  change. Do not wire `--update-snapshots` into the job.\n- **Per-PR versus nightly.** Per-PR in `web-e2e` is the natural home: +17 s on\n  a stack the job already has up, and a visual regression should block the PR\n  that caused it. WO-29's nightly is the alternative — in which case grep\n  `@visual` out of the `web-e2e` invocation so the skip does not sit in the log\n  forever.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `web/e2e/visual.spec.ts` | new — the 12-state table, the sweep, the inventory assertions, the determinism helper |\n| `web/e2e/__screenshots__/darwin/*.png` | new — 48 committed baselines |\n| `web/playwright.config.ts` | `@visual` joins `CHROMIUM_ONLY` (with its argument); `snapshotPathTemplate` with `{platform}` |\n| `web/package.json` | `e2e:visual`, `e2e:visual:update` |\n| `web/e2e/README.md` | the \"Visual regression (WO-28)\" section, the regeneration rule, the tags/projects/layout rows, the CI note |\n| `docs/revamp/evidence/gate-4/residual-risks.md` | new stub, RR-01 |\n\nNo product code, no lockfile, no workflow, no bookkeeping file and no gate-3\nevidence was touched.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
